\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Prediction-informed adaptive EKF system overview. SENTINEL produces a five-second advance degradation probability from GNSS signal features. After unsupervised floor calibration, this probability drives the measurement noise covariance schedule, causing the inertial dead-reckoning component to assume navigation authority before the corrupted fix arrives. NHC = non-holonomic constraint; ZUPT = zero-velocity update.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_overview}{{1}{2}{}{}{}}
